00:10:21.031 --> 00:10:22.280
That's a whole different framework.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:25.590
So regenerative agriculture
is a way of growing food,

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:26.835
it grows higher quality food,

00:10:26.835 --> 00:10:30.180
they build the soil with organic matter

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:32.170
that draws carbon out of the atmosphere.

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:33.300
Literally, most of the carbon,

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.950
a third of the carbon that's
in the atmosphere today

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:36.180
came from the destruction of our soil,

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:37.700
we can put it back in the soil.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:38.875
Better than rain forest.
- That's interesting.

00:10:38.875 --> 00:10:40.330
- So it'll help the soil,

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:42.038
it'll conserve water, we're losing,

00:10:42.038 --> 00:10:44.510
water scarcity is a huge
thing around the world

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.030
and we're seeing floods and droughts,

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:49.060
that can be solved by fixing
the soil through these methods.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:51.237
It actually can reduce the use
of pesticides, fertilizers,

00:10:51.237 --> 00:10:53.380
and all these harmful things.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:55.470
It's better for the animals
because they're grazing around,

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.900
it increases biodiversity,
our pollinators are dying,

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:01.470
75% are lost, bees and butterflies,

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.900
that can be rebuilt through
regenerative agriculture.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:05.647
So if you seek out foods from farms

00:11:05.647 --> 00:11:07.519
